WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.400
Let’s tie radar back to the Rules, because the exam asks it from both sides.

2
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:13.125
If your boat has radar, Rule seven says you must use it properly, including long-range scanning for early warning.

3
00:00:13.375 --> 00:00:16.500
Having it switched off in fog isn’t an option.

4
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.150
A target seen only on radar is not in sight.

5
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.275
That’s Rule three.

6
00:00:22.525 --> 00:00:25.450
So in fog, Rule nineteen governs.

7
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.975
For a target forward of your beam, what don’t you do?

8
00:00:29.975 --> 00:00:31.650
Turn to port.

9
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.975
Help the other fellow, too.

10
00:00:34.225 --> 00:00:39.675
A radar reflector, mounted as high as practical, makes your boat a better target.

11
00:00:39.925 --> 00:00:42.275
And practice on clear days.

12
00:00:42.525 --> 00:00:47.250
Compare the screen with what your eyes see, until you can read it without thinking.

13
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.450
That’s lesson twelve.

14
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.250
Steady on the E B L means risk.

15
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.775
Don’t tune out the real targets.

16
00:00:55.025 --> 00:00:56.900
Low beaches hide.

17
00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:59.150
Plot before you decide.

18
00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.425
Next time: weather.
